  "content": {
    "id": "p28-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Teams $A$ and $B$ play a series of games. To win the series, team $A$ must win one game, whereas team $B$ must win two games. The probability of team $A$ winning any game is $0.3$. Find the probability that:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p28-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "team $A$ wins the series",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.51$",
          "worked": "Team $A$ wins either the first game, or the second game after team $B$ wins the first.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\text{ wins the series})&=0.3+0.7\\times0.3\\\\P(A\\text{ wins the series})&=0.3+0.21\\\\P(A\\text{ wins the series})&=0.51\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "team $A$ won the series given that there were two games in the series.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.3$",
          "worked": "A two-game series occurs when team $B$ wins the first game. The possible paths are $BA$ and $BB$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(BA)&=0.7\\times0.3=0.21\\\\P(BB)&=0.7\\times0.7=0.49\\\\P(A\\text{ wins}\\mid\\text{two games})&=\\frac{0.21}{0.21+0.49}\\\\P(A\\text{ wins}\\mid\\text{two games})&=0.3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      }
    ]
  },
